					"name": "Unaging While Fed",
					"reference": "B95",
					"local_notes": "No aging rolls while fed. Replaces the Aeldari Extended Lifespan; a fed Drukhari has no natural end date at all.\n\nLore: Drukhari are as long-lived as any Aeldari, and the fed ones do not visibly age at all. The eldest Archons and Haemonculi are older than most craftworlds' oldest Exarchs, kept young by a steady diet of other people's agony. Starved Drukhari, by contrast, are described as withered and grey (Codex: Dark Eldar / Drukhari background).\n\nDesign: Unaging (B95, 15 points) with Accessibility (B110) -40%: it works only while the Soul Thirst dependency is met. 15 x 0.6 = 9 points. It stands in for the Aeldari Extended Lifespan (12 points) rather than adding to it.",
