		},
		{
			"id": "th5TgyIIS_sEPYcbp",
			"name": "Power from Pain (Stage I)",
			"reference": "B59",
			"local_notes": "High Pain Threshold, once feeding has begun. Stage I of three; each later stage needs the one before it. A stage lapses at the end of the scene.\n\nLore: Every Drukhari fights harder for the taste of blood. Codex background describes the Dark Eldar as growing bolder and stronger as the killing goes on, feeding on the pain they cause; the exact stages differ between Kabals, Wych Cults and Covens.\n\nDesign: High Pain Threshold (B59, 10 points) with Accessibility (B110) -30% for its trigger: 10 x 0.7 = 7 points. Deliberately no `attributes` feature: the bonus is conditional and must not raise the sheet's stats before the trigger.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mKYrA0hgb__E0NJDm",
					"name": "Accessibility",
					"reference": "B110",
					"local_notes": "Only after the Drukhari, or a comrade in the same unit, has drawn blood or caused real suffering in this scene.",
					"cost_adj": "-30%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "TaHsRb1LT5ptXgjwE",
			"name": "Power from Pain (Stage II)",
			"local_notes": "Stage II: melee and Fright Check bonuses (requires Stage I), lapses at the end of the scene.\n\nLore: By the time a fight has really turned, a Drukhari hits harder and cannot be frightened. Background: the Power from Pain rule in Codex: Drukhari (per unit, by kills scored).\n\nDesign: Melee and morale bonuses only; the real weight is small (5 + 2 = 7 points). Not `attributes`: the bonuses are conditional.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tN4JxSHVWmPWPhjIO",
					"name": "Bloodied Strength",
					"reference": "B88",
					"local_notes": "Striking ST +2: melee damage as if ST 2 higher.\n\nLore: The Kabalite's cruelty in melee sharpens as the blood flows.\n\nDesign: Striking ST 2 (B88, 5/level, 10) with Accessibility -50% = 5 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Drukhari"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mTBC5aAHOQeUmWaoT",
							"name": "Accessibility",
							"reference": "B110",
							"local_notes": "Only after Stage I plus at least one enemy dropped or seriously hurt in this scene by the Drukhari's unit.",
							"cost_adj": "-50%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2
				},
				{
					"id": "tP7jbRQAy8kaEFd0W",
					"name": "Bloodied Nerve",
					"reference": "B55",
					"local_notes": "Fearlessness +2 to Fright Checks.\n\nLore: A feeding Drukhari does not flinch from the things that break other people.\n\nDesign: Fearlessness 2 (B55, 2/level, 4) with Accessibility -50% = 2 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Drukhari"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mLHDxuliZzlZIHYqy",
							"name": "Accessibility",
							"reference": "B110",
							"local_notes": "Same trigger as Bloodied Strength.",
							"cost_adj": "-50%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 2,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tgf0ZQjLXUKCYt2Kd",
			"name": "Power from Pain (Stage III)",
			"reference": "B80",
			"local_notes": "Regeneration (Fast): 1 HP per minute (roughly 1 HP per 6 combat turns of 10 seconds when tracking turns).\n\nLore: The height of the feed: wounds close as fast as the killer can reopen new ones in other people. Codex: Drukhari's third stage is the strongest bonus a unit can earn.\n\nDesign: Regeneration, Fast tier (B80, 50 points, 1 HP per minute) with Accessibility -60%: 50 x 0.4 = 20 points. Kept at Fast rather than faster because the lore effect is 'hard to put down', not 'cannot be killed'.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "msBo-nUZj0bUnDmfQ",
					"name": "Accessibility",
					"reference": "B110",
					"local_notes": "Only after Stages I and II and at least three enemies dropped or badly hurt in this scene by the Drukhari's unit.",
					"cost_adj": "-60%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 50
		},
		{
			"id": "TGW3JhasTXsESY75t",
			"name": "Power from Pain",
			"local_notes": "Lore: All three stages together: the full Power from Pain a Drukhari of rank earns in a long fight.\n\nDesign: 7 + 7 + 20 = 34 points. Lower-tier templates include the single stages above instead.",
