		{
			"id": "t_S6Po2X8IMjETUJX",
			"name": "Haemonculus Regrowth",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "One Extra Life. On death, if a fragment reaches a Coven and the price is met, the character is regrown and returns, changed a little (GM's choice of small physical or mental side effect).\n\nLore: Haemonculi can regrow the dead from little more than a scrap, and the Covens sell that service to the powerful. Archons and their favoured servants are the ones who can afford the price, in coin, slaves or service. Codex: Drukhari background.\n\nDesign: Extra Life (B55, 25 points) with Accessibility (B110) -40% for the recovered-fragment and coven-fee requirements. 25 x 0.6 = 15 points. Reserved for Archons, favoured servants and Haemonculi; ordinary Kabalites and Wyches do not have it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mU8poN1lNweej2N3I",
					"name": "Accessibility",
					"reference": "B110",
					"local_notes": "Needs a body fragment (at least the head or a torso) recovered to a Haemonculus and a Coven paid for the work; lasts one life.",
					"cost_adj": "-40%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 25
		},
		{
			"id": "txjimqjdu2jQuhLOl",
			"name": "Sadism",
			"reference": "B152",
			"local_notes": "Takes pleasure in others' suffering and seeks chances to inflict it; roll self-control when the chance arises.\n\nLore: Cruelty is Commorragh's native culture, not a deviance. Most Drukhari, and every Haemonculus, take an openly aesthetic interest in others' pain (Codex: Drukhari and background across editions). The self-control 12 default represents someone who can hold off when it would cost them, e.g. in front of a superior.\n\nDesign: Sadism (B152, -15) with self-control 12.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -15,
			"cr": 12
		},
		{
			"id": "tD-WZYE6r5Xe1_Qvv",
			"name": "Callous",
			"reference": "B125",
			"local_notes": "Indifferent to others' pain; -3 reaction when it shows.\n\nLore: Even a Drukhari who does not enjoy suffering treats it as currency. Background.\n\nDesign: Callous (B125, -5).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "th_twunGL5D9qK1dH",
			"name": "Megalomania",
			"reference": "B144",
			"local_notes": "Believes they are destined to rule, and plans and boasts accordingly; -5 to resist flattery about their greatness.\n\nLore: Every Archon is scheming at the top of a Kabal and every Kabal is one betrayal from the next Archon. Background across Codex editions.\n\nDesign: Megalomania (B144, -10).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tOfH-BSsnVWxWt-Bq",
			"name": "Paranoia",
			"reference": "B148",
			"local_notes": "Assumes hidden plots against them; trusts nobody, with reason.\n\nLore: In Commorragh most of the plots against an Archon are real. Paranoia is a survival skill here, not a delusion.\n\nDesign: Paranoia (B148, -10).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "t84pvLhMKtrY7JRHW",
			"name": "Overconfidence",
			"reference": "B148",
			"local_notes": "Overrates their own ability and underrates opposition; self-control roll to hold back from a risky show of strength.\n\nLore: Arena stars, aerial raiders and Kabal nobles all believe themselves the best in the room. Background.\n\nDesign: Overconfidence (B148, -5) with self-control 12.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -5,
			"cr": 12
		},
		{
			"id": "tbna09FSgvA3-55Fa",
			"name": "Selfish",
			"reference": "B153",
			"local_notes": "Puts own gain over the group's; self-control roll to share loot or hold a post.\n\nLore: A Kabalite's loyalty is to their own advancement first. Background.\n\nDesign: Selfish (B153, -5) with self-control 12.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -5,
			"cr": 12
		},
		{
			"id": "tllDCqXoeIp2Ams4Y",
			"name": "Duty (Coven)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Bound to a Haemonculus's Coven: 12 or less on a frequency roll each session that the Coven requires service.\n\nLore: Wracks serve their Haemonculus because they cannot leave. Some were bought as slaves, some sold themselves in the hope of a better fate, and few are free to walk away. Background.\n\nDesign: Duty (B133) 12 or less, -10 points, not extremely hazardous.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "T9E1atZ_9Mj6Vdyc-",
			"name": "Combat Drug: Adrenalight",
			"local_notes": "One dose per combat. Enable the trait for the fight; lasts the whole fight (about ten minutes at most). Roll HT after the fight ends; on a failure lose 1 FP and take -1 on all rolls for an hour (the comedown).\n\nLore: Adrenalight is the Wych Cults' basic fighting stimulant: it makes a warrior faster, lets her strike more often, and is favoured for its low risk. Background: Codex: Drukhari's Wych Cult combat drugs list; the tabletop effect is one extra attack, translated here as more speed.\n\nDesign: Modest boost, no more than Aspect Training's own speed edge. Net cost 7 - 5 = 2 points when enabled.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tWy7p--lZ7J2Z0iOd",
					"name": "Adrenalight Surge",
					"local_notes": "Basic Speed +0.5.\n\nLore: A stimulant that speeds reactions and pushes the body to strike more often.\n\nDesign: Increased Basic Speed +0.5 (B17, 10 points) with the one-dose Accessibility -30%: 7 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Drukhari"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m-xsT3LBk9exym9XY",
							"name": "Accessibility",
							"reference": "B110",
							"local_notes": "One dose per combat; effect lasts the fight, then the comedown. ",
							"cost_adj": "-30%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_speed",
							"amount": 0.5
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t6C-t-5P4GM-tbBmt",
					"name": "Dependency (Adrenalight)",
					"reference": "B130",
					"local_notes": "Roll HT after the fight ends; on a failure lose 1 FP and take -1 on all rolls for an hour (the comedown).\n\nLore: Combat drugs are habit-forming; regular users need a dose or suffer the comedown.\n\nDesign: Dependency (B130), a Common substance in Commorragh, milder than Soul Thirst, priced at -5 as a judgement on B130's method.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Drukhari"
					],
					"base_points": -5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T5EKzrk4-BFm60n_E",
			"name": "Combat Drug: Grave Lotus",
			"local_notes": "One dose per combat. Enable the trait for the fight; lasts the whole fight (about ten minutes at most). Roll HT after the fight ends; on a failure lose 1 FP and take -1 on all rolls for an hour (the comedown).\n\nLore: Grave Lotus is the Wych's blade-fighting drug: it slows the world so that a strike is seen coming. Background: Codex: Drukhari's Wych Cult combat drug list; tabletop effect is +1 Weapon Skill.\n\nDesign: Hits skill, not damage. Net 6 - 5 = 1 point when enabled.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
