		{
			"id": "TMfLWJxBpqQhRK1d_",
			"name": "Combat Drug: Painbringer",
			"local_notes": "One dose per combat. Enable the trait for the fight; lasts the whole fight (about ten minutes at most). Roll HT after the fight ends; on a failure lose 1 FP and take -1 on all rolls for an hour (the comedown). The wounds it ignored still count: track HP as normal.\n\nLore: Painbringer numbs the nerves so that a fighter can ignore what would send her down. Background: Codex: Drukhari's Wych Cult drug list; tabletop effect is Feel No Pain.\n\nDesign: Overlaps with Power from Pain Stage I on purpose (the drug is the Wych's way of getting it earlier). Net 7 - 5 = 2 points when enabled.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tSLfEjLxxLVtuX9Wt",
					"name": "Painbringer Numbness",
					"reference": "B59",
					"local_notes": "High Pain Threshold. Does not stack with Power from Pain (Stage I).\n\nLore: A nerve-deadening drug: the Wych feels nothing until the fight is done and the damage arrives all at once.\n\nDesign: High Pain Threshold (B59, 10 points) with the one-dose Accessibility: 7 points.",
					"tags": [
